Manual edge cases (smoke-logs/manual-edge-tests/) — all PASS:
  edge1   — dialog grows from 3 to 4 buttons when an alternative model
            is installed; "Wybierz inny model" → combo + aider spawn
            with the chosen tag, no wizard / no relaunch.
  edge2   — "Pomiń" → spawn aider with the missing model (banner shows
            qwen2.5-coder:7b); next prompt would yield litellm error,
            but that's the contract the user accepted.
  edge3   — "Anuluj" → no wizard tab spawned, original aider tab stays
            empty, wmctrl reports `AiderBug2Test [2/2]`.
  edge4   — Tools → Configure local model (manual entry) → wizard pulls,
            saves options.json, exits — and NO aider auto-relaunch
            because the wizard ran without --session-id (so the sentinel
            it would write has no matching session_id for
            compute_relaunch_config). Verified by wmctrl `[2/2]` after
            wizard exit.
  edge5   — `r` refresh path: opened wizard, the picker prompt is
            "Choose a number, 'r' to refresh catalog, or 'c' for custom
            tag [1/2/3/4/5/6/7/r/c] (1):" — confirms the choices are
            wired in. Live refresh against GitHub raw observed in the
            smoke output of test_catalog_refresh.py:
            test_refresh_writes_cache_on_success.
